WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.950
California lies in earthquake country.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:07.830
Its law bans building for human
occupancy over an active fault.

3
00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:11.710
Sensors catch an earthquake's
fast P waves and send alerts,

4
00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:14.450
giving seconds to minutes of warning.

5
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:21.390
Yet in 2025, only 15.24 per cent of
homeowners' policies in California included

6
00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:22.890
earthquake cover.

7
00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:25.890
So why do most policies go without it?

8
00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:27.570
Don't people know the risk?

9
00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:28.970
Is the cover banned?

10
00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:32.630
In this mission, you'll sort
hazards into geophysical,

11
00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:36.930
atmospheric and hydrological,
and see how their impacts differ.

12
00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:39.530
Then you'll line up the
ways people respond,

13
00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:42.190
from doing almost nothing
to planned management,

14
00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:45.190
and test what shapes their choices.

15
00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:50.570
Your mission: explain why so few California
homeowners' policies include earthquake

16
00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:51.330
cover.
